ALGORITHM MVCWorkflow

START

1. User enters a URL or submits a request.

2. Send the request to the web server.

3. Controller receives the user request.

4. Controller identifies the requested operation.

5. Validate the request data.

6. IF the request data is invalid THEN
       Send an error message to the View.
       Display the error to the user.
       STOP
   END IF

7. Controller calls the appropriate Model.

8. Model processes the business logic.

9. Model establishes a connection with the database.

10. Model executes the required database operation.

11. IF database operation fails THEN
        Return an error to the Controller.
        Controller sends the error to the View.
        Display error message.
        STOP
    END IF

12. Retrieve the required data from the database.

13. Model sends the processed data to the Controller.

14. Controller passes the data to the View.

15. View generates the required webpage.

16. Send the generated response to the user's browser.

17. Display the result to the user.

END
